Cozempic was imported into this repository at commit 210b026 ("merge from
cozempic"), 21,700 lines of Python, and this project subsequently forked it
rather than keeping it as a vendored dependency. The reversal, and what it
costs, is recorded in docs/DECISIONS.md section 0. The rename is mapped in
docs/FORK.md.

The upstream git sha of the 1.8.39 release is not recorded here, because it was
not recorded at import and cannot be recovered from what was imported. Anyone
needing an exact diff against upstream should take it against the 1.8.39 source
distribution published on PyPI.

Derived code, by directory, as of the fork decision:

  src/winnow/legacy/
                   the whole of the imported tree, moved here by docs/FORK.md
                   phase 1 and renamed; it was src/cozempic/
  plugin/          hooks, skills and the MCP server
  npm/             scheduled for deletion, docs/FORK.md phase 2
  packaging/       scheduled for deletion, docs/FORK.md phase 2
  tests/           the suite that arrived with the tree
  docs/behavioral-digest-design.md, docs/qa-fleet.md
                   Cozempic's own design notes, arrived with the merge

Written by this project and not derived: src/winnow/cli.py,
src/winnow/orchestrator_safe.py and their tests, docs/SPEC.md, docs/DECISIONS.md,
docs/MILESTONES.md, docs/COZEMPIC.md, docs/USAGEFOUNDRY.md, docs/FORK.md,
README.md and this file.

CONTRIBUTORS.md credits the people who wrote the inherited code, by name and by
pull-request number. That attribution is not conditional on the code staying
unmodified and is not removable. It applies to code that is now winnow's, which
makes it more load-bearing rather than less.

